      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2007-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let the smaller integer be \\(x.\\) Then the larger is \\(x + 2,\\) and \\[ x + 2 = 3x, \\] so \\(x = 1.\\)\n\nThe two integers are \\(1\\) and \\(3,\\) and their sum is \\(4.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
